// Movement rules that are not a property of one unit archetype.
//
// `group_routing.lane_tolerance_permille`: group-consistent routing (plan
// `docs/plans/2026-11-10-group-routing.md`, D-7; owner answer Q0079, option 2; sanctioned
// deviation S-7 of plan `2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes`). Ground units given one Move or
// AttackMove command together take the lane (the side of every terrain obstacle) of the
// group's leader whenever that route is at most this many thousandths longer than the unit's
// own shortest route. 0 switches the rule off: every unit routes on its own, as in
// StarCraft II. Allowed range 0 to 1000.
//
// `pursuit.acquire_leash_radius`: a unit chasing a target it acquired by itself gives the chase up
// once it stands farther than this many world units from where the chase began (5.0.14 `CGame`
// `AcquireLeashRadius` 21, core GameData.xml:9 at 5444e12f13; plan
// `docs/plans/2026-11-18-contour-footprints.md` Amendment 4, B-142). 5.0.14's
// `AcquireLeashResetRadius` 5 and `AcquireMovementLimit` 21 (GameData.xml:10 and 8) are not
// modelled: what they do is not sourced (recorded in B-142). Whole world units, at least 1.
//
// `pursuit.follow_range_slop`: a unit following another (the follow order, plan
// `docs/plans/2026-11-26-follow-order.md` D-4) and resting by it walks again once its target stands
// more than this many world units from where it stood when the follower came to rest (5.0.14
// `CAbilMove` `FollowRangeSlop` 1, core AbilData.xml:1371-1377 at 5444e12f13; the Battlecruiser's
// own move ability has none, B-223). Whole world units, at least 0.
//
// `contact`: the contact rules of plan `docs/plans/2026-11-20-contact-solver.md` (§3.6; owner
// answer Q0092 (a); sanctioned deviations D-alpha and D-beta of
// `docs/questions/closed/0052-sanctioned-sc2-deviations.md`).
// - `pipeline`: the migration switch, Legacy (today's local movement) or Solver (intent steering
//   and the contact solver). Removed when the legacy pipeline is deleted (the plan's WP7).
// - `iterations` (C-3, plan Amendments 1 and 2): Jacobi iterations of the contact solver per tick:
//   the smallest count with at most 2 of 2,000 generated crowds ending with a friendly pair above
//   the moving bound and none above 8 %, each crowd a 9 x 9 hexagonal crowd standing in contact with
//   every body stepped by up to the catalog's worst injection rho (two jet_jumper bodies:
//   (s_a + s_b) / (r_a + r_b) = 0.56, s the top speed times the largest speed multiplier);
//   confirmed once on 1,000 unseen crowds (none above 5 %, worst 4.95 %). The test
//   `k_iterations_bring_injected_overlap_below_the_moving_bound` is its derivation. A second test
//   requires it to stay at least the closed-form bound ceil(ln(moving / rho) / ln(5/6)) (14).
// - `dead_band_permille` (C-4, D-alpha at rest): an overlap of at most this many thousandths of
//   the radius sum is not corrected; 1 % of the smallest radius sum (0.75) is 0.0075 world units.
// - `moving_overlap_permille` (D-alpha while moving): the bound `iterations` is derived for.
// - `side_horizon_factor` (I-3a): a threat counts from factor * (r + r_b) / speed ticks before
//   contact; 2 caps the side rule's turn at 30 degrees (sin = 1 / factor).
// - `moving_friends_push` (D-beta): moving friends push each other by priority (true), or each
//   yields its own approach (false).
// - `nudge_engaged_along_ring` (deviation D-delta, Q0095): allies may nudge an engaged melee unit
//   along its attack ring (its correction keeps only the part along the ring's tangent), never out
//   of range, never by enemies, never on Hold Position. On when absent.
// Validated at load: iterations >= 1, 0 < dead_band_permille < moving_overlap_permille < 1000,
// side_horizon_factor >= 1.
(
    group_routing: (
        lane_tolerance_permille: 75,
    ),
    pursuit: (
        acquire_leash_radius: 21,
        follow_range_slop: 1,
    ),
    contact: (
        pipeline: Solver,
        iterations: 21,
        dead_band_permille: 10,
        moving_overlap_permille: 50,
        side_horizon_factor: 2,
        moving_friends_push: true,
        nudge_engaged_along_ring: true,
    ),
)
